      "side": 1,
      "message": "Some general questions about this:\n1. The purpose of vconn_swap_counter is to prevent us from getting stuck in a VCS loop during cable discovery with a UFP that wants VCONN. How will this change affect that case? (I think it would leave us vulnerable to VCS forever.)\n2. Are we actually in G3 when this happens? I wouldn\u0027t expect the EC to be up in that case. If we\u0027re in S5 or higher, I would have thought we would be able to supply VCONN.\n3. Is the inability to supply VCONN in a low power state board-specific? If so, should this code be board-specific in some way?",
